ENTRY            23621   20251126   20260826   20260826       2323
SUBENT        23621001   20251126   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                  9         24
TITLE      Neutron total and capture cross-section measurement
           and  resolved resonance analysis of Er
AUTHOR     (G.Rovira,A.Kimura,S.Nakamura,S.Endo,O.Iwamoto,
            N.Iwamoto,T.Katabuchi)
INSTITUTE  (2JPNJAE,2JPNTIT)
REFERENCE  (J,ANE,225,111688,2026)
           #doi:10.1016/j.anucene.2025.111688
FACILITY   (SYNCH,2JPNJAE) ANNRI(BL04) beamline of MLF at J-PARC.
INC-SOURCE (SPALL) Spallation reaction in a mercury target
           irradiated with 3-GeV protons (740 kW).
           The proton beams were supplied at a repetition rate
           of 25 Hz and in the "double-bunch mode", in which
           two consecutive 100 ns-wide proton bunches were shot
           to produce neutrons with a time difference of 600 ns.
           Produced neutrons were slowed down in a supercritical
           para-hydrogen moderator.
REL-REF    (I,,K.Kino+,J,NIM/A,736,66,2014)
           Energy resolution of the pulsed neutron was given.
           (R,,Y.Danon+,J,NSE,128,61,1998)
           The fitted function and the fitted parameters for
           paramagnetic cross-section of nat-Er were given.
HISTORY    (20251107R) Numerical data was obtained from AUTHOR.
           (20251117C) Compiled by A.Kimura.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by AUTHOR. (2025-11-25)
ENDBIB              24
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           27
SUBENT        23621002   20251126   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                  8         30
REACTION   (68-ER-0(N,TOT),,TRN)
METHOD     (TRN,TOF)
SAMPLE     A 0.05-mm-thick nat-Er metal foil with an area density
           of 1.48+-0.02 x 10E-4 [atoms/b].
DETECTOR   (GLASD) A 6Li(>95%) enriched Li-glass detector
            -Scintillator: GS-20, manufactured by Saint Gobain
            -Size: 50 mm x 50 mm and a thickness of 1 mm
            -PMT: HAMAMATSU H7195
            -Flight length: 28.7 m
            -DAQ: CAEN V1720 (12bit, 250MHz)
            For background estimation, same size 7Li(>99.99%)
            loaded glass detector (GS-30:Saint Gobain) was used.
ANALYSIS   Frame-overlap and constant backgrounds were estimated
           using the operational pattern of J-PARC.
           Backgrounds due to gamma-rays were deduced using the
           result of the 7Li-glass detector.
CORRECTION The dead-time correction was applied using the
           extended dead-time model (416 +- 4 nano second) .
           The effect from paramagnetic scattering was removed.
           The paramagnetic cross-section for nat-Er was taken
           from the work of Danon et al. (See REL-REF.)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty.
           (ERR-S) Statistical uncertainty.
           (ERR-1) Uncertainty due to the neutron intensity.
           (ERR-2) Uncertainty due to the gamma-ray background.
           (ERR-3) Uncertainty due to the dead-time correction.
STATUS     (TABLE,,G.Rovira+,J,ANE,225,111688,2026)
            Fig. 7 in the REFERENCE.
           (COREL,23621003) Data for 0.175-mm-thick sample
           (COREL,23621004) Data for 1-mm-thick sample
ENDBIB              30
COMMON               1          3
THICKNESS
ATOMS/B
    1.48E-4
ENDCOMMON            3
