BIB                  8         33
REACTION   (68-ER-0(N,TOT),,SIG)
METHOD     (TRN,TOF)
SAMPLE     A 1-mm-thick nat-Er metal plate with an area
           density of 3.40+-0.05 x 10E-3 [atoms/b].
DETECTOR   (GLASD) A 6Li(>95%) enriched Li-glass detector
            -Scintillator: GS-20, manufactured by Saint Gobain
            -Size: 50 mm x 50 mm and a thickness of 1 mm
            -PMT: HAMAMATSU H7195
            -Flight length: 28.7 m
            -DAQ: CAEN V1720 (12bit, 250MHz)
            For background estimation, same size 7Li(>99.99%)
            loaded glass detector (GS-30:Saint Gobain) was used.
ANALYSIS   Frame-overlap and constant backgrounds were estimated
           using the operational pattern of J-PARC.
           Backgrounds due to gamma-rays were deduced using the
           result of the 7Li-glass detector.
CORRECTION The dead-time correction was applied using the
           extended dead-time model (416 +- 4 nano second) .
           The effect from paramagnetic scattering was removed.
           The paramagnetic cross-section for nat-Er was taken
           from the work of Danon et al. (See REL-REF.)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty.
           (ERR-S) Statistical uncertainty.
           (ERR-1) Uncertainty due to the neutron intensity.
           (ERR-2) Uncertainty due to the gamma-ray background.
           (ERR-3) Uncertainty due to the dead-time correction.
           (ERR-4) Uncertainty due to the area density of
                   the sample.
STATUS     (TABLE,,G.Rovira+,J,ANE,225,111688,2026)
            Fig.23 in the REFERENCE.
           (DEP,23621004) Raw Transmission Ratio.
           (COREL,23621005) Data for 0.05-mm-thick sample
           (COREL,23621006) Data for 0.175-mm-thick sample
ENDBIB              33
