ENDSUBENT        10534
SUBENT        23621008   20251126   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                  8         49
REACTION   (68-ER-0(N,G),,SIG)
METHOD     (TOF,PHWT)
SAMPLE     A 25-um-thick natural Er metal foil with a diameter of
           20 mm, a mass of 352.31 +- 0.01 mg and an area density
           of 7.28 +- 0.07 x 10E-5 [atom/b].
           An enriched B-10 sample was used for neutron spectrum
           measurement.
           Carbon samples were used to estimate the scattered
           neutron background.
           An Au foil sample with a thickness of 0.1-mm was used
           for normalization.
DETECTOR   (NAICR)
            -Size: 330 mm (diam.) and 203 mm in thickness
            -Angle: 90 deg with respect to the neutron beam line
            -Flight length: 27.9 m
            -DAQ: CAEN V1720 Digitizer (12bit, 250MHz)
ANALYSIS   Pulse-height weighting technique (PHWT) was applied
           with considering the natural abundance and the binding
           energy of each Er isotope.
           Measurements with the carbon samples and
           "Blank (no sample) " were used for background
           estimation.
           The relative neutron spectrum was estimated using the
           boron sample.
           The weighting function was normalized by comparing
           the experimental results of the Au sample at the 1st
           resonance using the saturated resonance method.
CORRECTION The dead-time correction was applied with the
           extended dead-time model. Correction factors for
           self-shielding and multiple scattering effects were
           deduced using the Monte-Carlo simulation code PHITS.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty
           (ERR-S) Statistical uncertainty
           (ERR-1) Uncertainty due to the frame-overlap
                   subtraction
           (ERR-2) Uncertainty due to the neutron flux
           (ERR-3) Uncertainty due to the deadtime correction
           (ERR-4) Uncertainty due to the self-shielding and
                   multiple scattering correction
           (ERR-5) Uncertainty due to the normalization
           (ERR-6) Uncertainty due to the weighting function
                   calculation
           (ERR-7) Uncertainty due to the PHWT (influence of
                   thresh hold energy)
           (ERR-8) Uncertainty due to the sample area density
STATUS     (TABLE,,G.Rovira+,J,ANE,225,111688,2026)
            Fig. 25 in the REFERENCE.
            Data were obtained from AUTHOR.
           (COREL,23621009) Data taken with Ge detector
ENDBIB              49
