ENDSUBENT         8372
SUBENT        23621009   20251126   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                 10         48
REACTION   (68-ER-0(N,G),,SIG)
METHOD     (TOF,PHWT)
SAMPLE     A 25-um-thick natural Er metal foil with a diameter of
           5 mm, a mass of 40.7 +- 0.01 mg and an area density
           of 7.42 +- 0.07 x 10E-5 [atom/b].
           An enriched B-10 sample was used for neutron spectrum
           measurement.
           A carbon samples was used to estimate the scattered
           neutron background.
           An Au foil sample with a thickness of 0.03-mm was used
           for normalization.
DETECTOR   (GE) An array of Ge detector consists of two cluster-
           Ge detectors and eight coaxial-Ge detectors.
           DAQ: CAEN V1724 Digitizer (14bit, 100MHz)
ANALYSIS   Pulse-height weighting technique (PHWT) was applied
           with considering the natural abundance and the binding
           energy of each Er isotope.
           Measurements with the carbon sample and
           "Blank (no sample) " were used for background
           estimation.
           The relative neutron spectrum was estimated using the
           boron sample.
           The weighting function was normalized at the thermal
           energy point using the experimental results of the Au
           sample and the recommended value from JENDL-5.0.
CORRECTION The dead-time correction was applied.
           Correction factors for self-shielding and multiple
           scattering effects were deduced using the Monte-Carlo
           simulation code PHITS.
MONITOR    (79-AU-197(N,G)79-AU-198,,SIG)
MONIT-REF  (,,3,JENDL-5,,2021)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty
           (ERR-S) Statistical uncertainty
           (ERR-1) Uncertainty due to the frame-overlap
                   subtraction
           (ERR-2) Uncertainty due to the neutron flux
           (ERR-3) Uncertainty due to the deadtime correction
           (ERR-4) Uncertainty due to the self-shielding and
                   multiple scattering correction
           (ERR-5) Uncertainty due to the normalization
           (ERR-6) Uncertainty due to the weighting function
                   calculation
           (ERR-7) Uncertainty due to the PHWT (influence of
                   thresh hold energy)
           (ERR-8) Uncertainty due to the sample area density
STATUS     (TABLE,,G.Rovira+,J,ANE,225,111688,2026)
            Fig.24 in the REFERENCE.
           (COREL,23621008) Data taken with NaI detector
ENDBIB              48
