BIB                  5         34
REACTION  1(68-ER-167(N,0),,EN)
          2(68-ER-167(N,G),,WID,,RM)
          3(68-ER-167(N,EL),,WID,,RM)
ASSUMED    (ASSUM,68-ER-167(N,G),,WID,,RM)
ANALYSIS   (SHAPE) Resonance parameters were determined from a
           resonance shape analysis with the REFIT code.
           - A combined fit of the capture cross-sections and the
             transmission ratios, after removing the influence of
             paramagnetic neutron scattering, were employed up to
             65 eV.
           - The ANNRI beamline resolution function was taken
             from the work of Kino. See REL-REF.
           - The initial resonance parametrization data were
             taken from JENDL-5.
           - A negative resonance was added to fit the thermal
             region.
           - Above 43 eV, the values of the radiative width were
             fixed to the average value of those below 43 eV
             resonances.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) The uncertainty of resonance energy was
           deduced from the uncertainty of the fitting result by
           REFIT, the flight length, and the initial time delay.
           The other uncertainties are the ones provided by REFIT.
